  "chapter": 566,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 34 Chapter 566\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 9686, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  banking  law, in relation to what mortgage\n        applicants need to know pamphlet on residential mortgages\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the creation  and  publication  of  the  \"what\nmortgage  applicants  need to know\" pamphlet, which would be provided to\nconsumers by mortgage lenders and bankers.\n \n  I support the goals of this legislation, which aims  to  increase  the\ninformation  consumers  have  as  they  make a major financial decision.\nHowever, technical  changes  are  necessary  to  ensure  the  disclosure\nrequirements  account for the varying requirements that apply to differ-\nent residential mortgage products.\n\n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
